      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Automated Car Accident Insurance Claim\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow automates car accident insurance claim intake from a form submission through policy validation, photo authenticity checks, AI visit assessment, and field-team dispatch. It verifies the claimant\u2019s policy in Google Sheets, rejects invalid policies with a Slack alert, and enriches valid claims with image metadata and dispatch details. It then uses external AI services to flag suspicious photos, assess whether a field visit is needed, notify the field team in Slack, and log the visit in Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Insurance Claim Intake Form fields to collect policy details, claimant contact information, accident location, and the accident image upload.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and point the policy verification and visit logging nodes to the correct spreadsheets, worksheets, and lookup/logging columns.\n- Connect Slack credentials and select the channels or users for invalid-policy alerts, photo-review alerts, and field-team dispatch notifications.\n- Configure the HTTP request credentials or headers for the AI image authenticity endpoint, including any required API key.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for the AI Visit Assessment agent and confirm the structured output parser schema matches the expected dispatch assessment fields.\n- Review the custom code nodes to ensure they reference the correct binary image property names and form field names.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the authenticity scoring thresholds, Slack message templates, dispatch record fields, and AI assessment prompt/schema to match your claims process and escalation rules."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f35b0ee0-2779-4bcd-9d4d-d76a7303af52",
